					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465390#post-2703682</guid>
				<title>Today I found out that fish yawn too.</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465390/scp-222-j#post-2703682</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 05 Dec 2016 05:21:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Today I got myself a new betta fish. Kylo Ren is a lovely red crowntail who gets mad at lots of things.</p> <p>Also he's already gotten used to my face and my voice and every time I sit by his tank for a few minutes he starts swimming up near the surface and looking upwards expectantly like &quot;human, where is my food&quot; and I just look at him all &quot;Kylo, you already ate today&quot;.</p> <p>The most recent time we had this exchange he actually yawned at me and looked away.</p> <p>I think I just got dissed by a fish.</p> <p>Anyway, apparently there's a photographer/diver who likes capturing fish yawns on camera: <a href="http://www.divephotoguide.com/underwater-photography-special-features/article/photographing-fish-yawns/">http://www.divephotoguide.com/underwater-photography-special-features/article/photographing-fish-yawns/</a></p> <p>ETA: this is exactly what Kylo Ren fish did to me: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9VHKZ4hunHs">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9VHKZ4hunHs</a></p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
