					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465390#post-2078405</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-465390/scp-222-j#post-2078405</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 31 Jul 2014 04:48:22 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Koekr8144</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1649893</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I've read this multiple times before, though never finished it, and for all those times I wasn't entertained or amused in any way. I just saw it as another joke scp about something mundane that the foundation calls an SCP for no good reason, and an unfunny one at that. Written well, but not funny.</p> <p>That is, until I checked the last line</p> <blockquote> <p>Addendum: Recent research has concluded that SCP-222-J can not only be transmitted through visual stimuli, but through writing as well.</p> </blockquote> <p>Then it all clicked into place.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
